      "headline": "Start of the Battle of Gettysburg",
      "text": "The Battle of Gettysburg began on July 1, 1863, when Confederate forces under General Robert E. Lee clashed with Union forces led by Major General George G. Meade in and around the town of Gettysburg, Pennsylvania.",
      "date": "1863-07-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Second Day of Battle",
      "text": "On July 2, 1863, the battle continued with heavy fighting at locations such as Little Round Top, the Wheatfield, and Devil's Den. Both sides suffered significant casualties.",
      "date": "1863-07-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Pickett's Charge",
      "text": "On July 3, 1863, the final day of the Battle of Gettysburg, Confederate General Lee ordered an assault known as Pickett's Charge against the center of the Union line on Cemetery Ridge. The charge was repelled with heavy Confederate losses.",
      "date": "1863-07-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Battle of Gettysburg",
      "text": "The Battle of Gettysburg concluded on July 3, 1863, with a Union victory. The battle resulted in over 50,000 combined casualties and marked a turning point in the American Civil War.",
      "date": "1863-07-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Gettysburg Address",
      "text": "On November 19, 1863, President Abraham Lincoln delivered the Gettysburg Address at the dedication of the Soldiers' National Cemetery in Gettysburg, Pennsylvania, honoring the fallen and redefining the purpose of the war.",
      "date": "1863-11-19"
    }
  ]
}

