      "headline": "Abduction of James Bulger",
      "text": "On 1993-02-12, two 10-year-old boys, Robert Thompson and Jon Venables, abducted two-year-old James Patrick Bulger from the New Strand Shopping Centre in Bootle, Merseyside.",
      "date": "1993-02-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Murder of James Bulger",
      "text": "On 1993-02-12, after abducting him, Thompson and Venables tortured and murdered James Bulger. His body was left on a railway line in Walton, Liverpool.",
      "date": "1993-02-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discovery of James Bulger's Body",
      "text": "On 1993-02-14, James Bulger's mutilated body was discovered on a railway line in Walton, Liverpool, two days after his abduction and murder.",
      "date": "1993-02-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Arrest of Robert Thompson and Jon Venables",
      "text": "On 1993-02-20, Robert Thompson and Jon Venables were arrested in connection with the abduction and murder of James Bulger.",
      "date": "1993-02-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Trial of Thompson and Venables",
      "text": "The trial of Robert Thompson and Jon Venables began on 1993-11-01. They were tried as adults, and the trial lasted 17 days.",
      "date": "1993-11-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Conviction of Thompson and Venables",
      "text": "On 1993-11-24, Robert Thompson and Jon Venables were found guilty of the murder of James Bulger. They became the youngest convicted murderers in modern British history.",
      "date": "1993-11-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sentencing of Thompson and Venables",
      "text": "On 1993-11-24, following their conviction, Robert Thompson and Jon Venables were sentenced to be detained at Her Majesty's pleasure, with a recommended minimum term of eight years.",
      "date": "1993-11-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of Thompson and Venables",
      "text": "In June 2001, Robert Thompson and Jon Venables were released on a lifelong licence after serving eight years in custody. They were given new identities to protect them from vigilante attacks.",
      "date": "2001-06"
    }
  ]
}

