    },
    {
      "headline": "Saqifah Event",
      "text": "Shortly after the death of Muhammad in 632, the Saqifah event took place where Abu Bakr was appointed as the first caliph by a group of early Muslims. This event marked the beginning of the Sunni tradition of electing a caliph.",
