      "text": "In 1809, Byron published 'English Bards and Scotch Reviewers', a satirical poem that gained him initial fame.",
      "date": "1809"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Grand Tour of Europe",
      "text": "Byron embarked on a grand tour of Europe from 1809 to 1811, visiting countries such as Portugal, Spain, Malta, Albania, and Greece.",
      "date": "1809"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Childe Harold's Pilgrimage'",
      "text": "In 1812, Byron published the first two cantos of 'Childe Harold's Pilgrimage', which brought him widespread acclaim.",
      "date": "1812"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marriage to Annabella Milbanke",
      "text": "Byron married Annabella Milbanke on January 2, 1815. The marriage was short-lived, and they separated in 1816.",
      "date": "1815-01-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Birth of Daughter, Ada Lovelace",
      "text": "Byron's daughter, Ada Lovelace, was born on December 10, 1815. She would later become a pioneering figure in computing.",
      "date": "1815-12-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exile from England",
      "text": "In 1816, Byron left England due to mounting debts and scandals, never to return.",
      "date": "1816"
    },
