      "headline": "Discovery of the Azores",
      "text": "The Azores were discovered by Portuguese navigators in the early 15th century, around 1427. The islands were uninhabited at the time of their discovery.",
      "date": "1427"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Settlement Begins",
      "text": "The settlement of the Azores began in 1439, with the arrival of settlers from mainland Portugal.",
      "date": "1439"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of Captaincies",
      "text": "In 1443, the islands were divided into captaincies, which were granted to Portuguese nobles to govern and develop.",
      "date": "1443"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Salga",
      "text": "The Battle of Salga took place on July 25, 1581, during the Portuguese succession crisis, where the Azorean forces successfully defended against Spanish invaders.",
      "date": "1581-07-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Azores under Spanish Rule",
      "text": "From 1580 to 1640, the Azores were under Spanish rule as part of the Iberian Union, following the Portuguese succession crisis.",
      "date": "1580"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Restoration of Portuguese Independence",
      "text": "In 1640, the Portuguese Restoration War led to the end of Spanish rule, and the Azores returned to Portuguese control.",
      "date": "1640"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Liberal Wars",
      "text": "During the Liberal Wars (1828-1834), the Azores were a stronghold for the liberal forces against the absolutists.",
      "date": "1828"
    },
