      "headline": "Unauthorized Takeoff",
      "text": "Richard Russell performed an unauthorized takeoff from Sea–Tac Airport, prompting immediate response from air traffic control and military forces.",
      "date": "2018-08-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "F-15 Fighters Scrambled",
      "text": "Two McDonnell Douglas F-15 Eagle fighters were scrambled to intercept the stolen aircraft shortly after it took off.",
      "date": "2018-08-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Radio Contact with Russell",
      "text": "Sea–Tac air traffic control made radio contact with Russell, who was the sole occupant of the aircraft. During the communication, Russell described himself as a 'broken guy, got a few screws loose, I guess.'",
      "date": "2018-08-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Barrel Roll Executed",
      "text": "Approximately 1 hour and 15 minutes after takeoff, Russell successfully executed a barrel roll with the aircraft, showcasing unexpected piloting skills.",
      "date": "2018-08-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Crash on Ketron Island",
      "text": "The aircraft crashed on lightly populated Ketron Island in Puget Sound, resulting in the death of Richard Russell, the only person on board.",
