      "text": "In 1856, K2 was first surveyed by the Great Trigonometric Survey of British India. The mountain was labeled as 'K2' because it was the second peak measured in the Karakoram Range.",
      "date": "1856"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Attempt to Climb K2",
      "text": "The first serious attempt to climb K2 was made in 1902 by an Anglo-Swiss expedition led by Oscar Eckenstein and Aleister Crowley. The team reached an altitude of 6,525 meters (21,407 ft) but did not succeed in reaching the summit.",
      "date": "1902"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Successful Ascent of K2",
      "text": "On July 31, 1954, an Italian expedition led by Ardito Desio successfully reached the summit of K2. Achille Compagnoni and Lino Lacedelli were the first climbers to reach the top.",
      "date": "1954-07-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Ascent of K2 in Winter",
      "text": "On January 16, 2021, a team of Nepali climbers made the first successful winter ascent of K2. This was a significant achievement as K2 was the last of the 14 eight-thousanders to be climbed in winter.",
      "date": "2021-01-16"
    }
  ]
}

