      "text": "In the early 18th century, Peter the Great implemented reforms that modernized the Russian language, including the introduction of the civil script.",
      "date": "1700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Russian Language Standardization",
      "text": "In the 18th and 19th centuries, the Russian language underwent significant standardization, influenced by the works of writers like Pushkin and Lomonosov.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Russian as Official Language of the Soviet Union",
      "text": "Following the formation of the Soviet Union in 1922, Russian became the de facto and de jure official language of the state.",
