      "headline": "Birth of C. V. Raman",
      "text": "C. V. Raman was born on November 7, 1888, in Tiruchirappalli, Madras Presidency, British India.",
      "date": "1888-11-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Graduation from Presidency College",
      "text": "In 1904, Raman graduated with a Bachelor of Arts degree from Presidency College, University of Madras, where he stood first and won a gold medal in physics.",
      "date": "1904"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Master's Degree",
      "text": "In 1907, Raman completed his Master of Arts degree from the University of Madras, again excelling in his studies.",
      "date": "1907"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Joined Indian Finance Service",
      "text": "In 1907, Raman joined the Indian Finance Service as an Assistant Accountant General in Calcutta.",
      "date": "1907"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Research at Indian Association for the Cultivation of Science",
      "text": "While working in Calcutta, Raman began conducting research at the Indian Association for the Cultivation of Science (IACS) in 1907.",
      "date": "1907"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discovery of the Raman Effect",
      "text": "On February 28, 1928, C. V. Raman discovered the Raman Effect, a phenomenon of light scattering, which later earned him the Nobel Prize in Physics.",
      "date": "1928-02-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nobel Prize in Physics",
      "text": "In 1930, C. V. Raman was awarded the Nobel Prize in Physics for his work on the scattering of light and for the discovery of the Raman Effect.",
      "date": "1930"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Knighted by the British Government",
      "text": "In 1929, C. V. Raman was knighted by the British Government for his contributions to science.",
      "date": "1929"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Director of Indian Institute of Science",
      "text": "In 1933, Raman became the first Indian director of the Indian Institute of Science in Bangalore.",
      "date": "1933"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Founded the Raman Research Institute",
      "text": "In 1948, C. V. Raman founded the Raman Research Institute in Bangalore, where he continued his research until his death.",
      "date": "1948"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of C. V. Raman",
      "text": "C. V. Raman passed away on November 21, 1970, in Bangalore, India.",
      "date": "1970-11-21"
    }
  ]
}

