      "headline": "French Settlement",
      "text": "In 1764, the French established a settlement at Port Louis on East Falkland.",
      "date": "1764"
    },
    {
      "headline": "British Settlement",
      "text": "In 1765, the British established a settlement at Port Egmont on Saunders Island.",
      "date": "1765"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Spanish Control",
      "text": "In 1770, Spain expelled the British from Port Egmont, but the British returned in 1771.",
      "date": "1770"
    },
    {
      "headline": "British Withdrawal",
      "text": "In 1774, the British withdrew from the islands due to economic pressures, leaving a plaque asserting their claim.",
      "date": "1774"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Spanish Abandonment",
      "text": "Spain abandoned its settlement in 1811, leaving the islands without a permanent population.",
      "date": "1811"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Argentine Claim",
      "text": "In 1820, the United Provinces of the River Plate (later Argentina) claimed the islands and established a settlement in 1828.",
      "date": "1820"
    },
    {
      "headline": "British Reassertion",
      "text": "In 1833, the British reasserted their claim and expelled the Argentine military presence.",
      "date": "1833"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Falklands War",
      "text": "In 1982, Argentina invaded the Falkland Islands, leading to a conflict with the United Kingdom known as the Falklands War. The UK regained control after a 10-week conflict.",
      "date": "1982"
    },
