      "text": "In the late 9th century, the area that is now Budapest was settled by the Magyars, marking the beginning of Hungarian history in the region.",
      "date": "0896"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Mention of Buda",
      "text": "The first known reference to the city of Buda was in 1148, indicating its existence as a significant settlement.",
      "date": "1148"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mongol Invasion",
      "text": "In 1241, the Mongols invaded Hungary, causing significant destruction to the area, including the settlements that would become Budapest.",
      "date": "1241"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Buda Becomes Capital",
      "text": "In 1361, Buda was declared the capital of the Kingdom of Hungary.",
      "date": "1361"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ottoman Occupation",
      "text": "In 1541, Buda was captured by the Ottoman Empire, beginning a period of occupation that lasted until 1686.",
      "date": "1541"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Liberation from Ottomans",
      "text": "In 1686, Buda was liberated from Ottoman rule by the Holy League, marking the end of Ottoman control.",
      "date": "1686"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Unification of Buda, Pest, and Óbuda",
      "text": "On November 17, 1873, the cities of Buda, Pest, and Óbuda were officially unified to form Budapest.",
      "date": "1873-11-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Austro-Hungarian Compromise",
      "text": "In 1867, the Austro-Hungarian Compromise was enacted, leading to the establishment of the dual monarchy of Austria-Hungary, with Budapest as a co-capital.",
      "date": "1867"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World War II and Siege of Budapest",
      "text": "From December 1944 to February 1945, Budapest was besieged by Soviet forces, resulting in significant destruction.",
      "date": "1944-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "1956 Hungarian Revolution",
      "text": "In October 1956, Budapest was the focal point of the Hungarian Revolution against Soviet-imposed policies, which was eventually crushed by Soviet forces.",
      "date": "1956-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Communist Rule",
      "text": "In 1989, Hungary transitioned from a communist state to a democratic republic, with Budapest as its capital.",
      "date": "1989"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Accession to the European Union",
      "text": "On May 1, 2004, Hungary, with Budapest as its capital, became a member of the European Union.",
      "date": "2004-05-01"
