      "headline": "Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant Accident Begins",
      "text": "On 11 March 2011, the Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant experienced a major nuclear accident due to the earthquake and tsunami, which caused electrical grid failure and damaged backup energy sources.",
      "date": "2011-03-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reactor Cooling Failure",
      "text": "Following the earthquake and tsunami on 11 March 2011, the inability to sufficiently cool the reactors after shutdown compromised containment, leading to the release of radioactive contaminants.",
      "date": "2011-03-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "International Nuclear Event Scale Rating",
      "text": "The Fukushima nuclear accident was rated seven on the International Nuclear Event Scale by the Nuclear and Industrial Safety Agency, following a report by the JNES. This rating was given due to the severity of the incident.",
      "date": "2011"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Comparison to Chernobyl Disaster",
      "text": "The Fukushima nuclear accident is regarded as the worst nuclear incident since the Chernobyl disaster in 1986, which was also rated a seven on the International Nuclear Event Scale.",
      "date": "2011"
    }
  ]
}

