      "text": "On January 18, 1701, Frederick I crowned himself King in Prussia, marking the establishment of the Kingdom of Prussia.",
      "date": "1701-01-18"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Frederick William I's Reign",
      "text": "Frederick William I, known as the 'Soldier King', reigned from 1713 to 1740. He centralized the government and expanded the military.",
      "date": "1713"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Frederick the Great's Reign",
      "text": "Frederick II, known as Frederick the Great, reigned from 1740 to 1786. He expanded Prussian territories and established Prussia as a major European power.",
      "date": "1740"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Seven Years' War",
      "text": "From 1756 to 1763, Prussia was involved in the Seven Years' War, which solidified its status as a great power in Europe.",
      "date": "1756"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Partition of Poland",
      "text": "Prussia participated in the First Partition of Poland in 1772, acquiring significant territories.",
      "date": "1772"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Napoleonic Wars",
      "text": "Prussia was involved in the Napoleonic Wars from 1806 to 1815, suffering initial defeats but later contributing to Napoleon's defeat.",
      "date": "1806"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Congress of Vienna",
      "text": "In 1815, the Congress of Vienna redefined the map of Europe after the Napoleonic Wars, strengthening Prussia's position.",
      "date": "1815"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Revolutions of 1848",
      "text": "Prussia faced internal unrest during the Revolutions of 1848, leading to some liberal reforms.",
      "date": "1848"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Austro-Prussian War",
      "text": "In 1866, Prussia defeated Austria in the Austro-Prussian War, leading to the exclusion of Austria from German affairs.",
      "date": "1866"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Unification of Germany",
      "text": "On January 18, 1871, the German Empire was proclaimed in the Hall of Mirrors at the Palace of Versailles, with Prussia as its leading state.",
      "date": "1871-01-18"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Kingdom of Prussia",
      "text": "The Kingdom of Prussia was dissolved in 1918 following Germany's defeat in World War I and the abdication of Kaiser Wilhelm II.",
      "date": "1918"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "timeline": [
    {
      "headline": "Proposal of the Fourteenth Amendment",
      "text": "The Fourteenth Amendment to the United States Constitution was proposed on June 13, 1866, in response to issues related to formerly enslaved Americans following the American Civil War.",
      "date": "1866-06-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption of the Fourteenth Amendment",
      "text": "The Fourteenth Amendment was adopted on July 9, 1868, as one of the Reconstruction Amendments. It addresses citizenship rights and equal protection under the law.",
