      "text": "The Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) was established on July 26, 1908, as the Bureau of Investigation (BOI). It was created by Attorney General Charles Bonaparte during the presidency of Theodore Roosevelt.",
      "date": "1908-07-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Renaming to Federal Bureau of Investigation",
      "text": "In 1935, the Bureau of Investigation was renamed the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI). This change reflected its growing role in federal law enforcement and intelligence.",
      "date": "1935"
    },
    {
      "headline": "J. Edgar Hoover's Tenure as Director",
      "text": "J. Edgar Hoover served as the first Director of the FBI from its establishment in 1935 until his death in 1972. His tenure was marked by the expansion of the FBI's powers and influence.",
      "date": "1935"
    },
    {
      "headline": "COINTELPRO Initiation",
      "text": "The FBI initiated the COINTELPRO (Counter Intelligence Program) in 1956, aimed at surveilling, infiltrating, discrediting, and disrupting domestic political organizations deemed subversive.",
      "date": "1956"
    },
    {
      "headline": "FBI's Role in Civil Rights Movement",
      "text": "During the 1960s, the FBI played a controversial role in the Civil Rights Movement, including surveillance of civil rights leaders like Martin Luther King Jr.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Watergate Investigation",
      "text": "The FBI was involved in the investigation of the Watergate scandal, which led to the resignation of President Richard Nixon in 1974.",
      "date": "1972"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Creation of the Hostage Rescue Team",
      "text": "In 1983, the FBI established the Hostage Rescue Team (HRT), a specialized counter-terrorism unit.",
      "date": "1983"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Oklahoma City Bombing Investigation",
      "text": "The FBI led the investigation into the Oklahoma City bombing on April 19, 1995, which was the deadliest act of domestic terrorism in U.S. history at the time.",
      "date": "1995-04-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "September 11 Attacks and FBI's Role",
      "text": "Following the September 11, 2001 attacks, the FBI shifted its focus to counterterrorism and played a key role in the investigation and response.",
      "date": "2001-09-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Creation of the Cyber Division",
      "text": "In 2002, the FBI created the Cyber Division to address the growing threat of cybercrime and cyberterrorism.",
      "date": "2002"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Boston Marathon Bombing Investigation",
      "text": "The FBI led the investigation into the Boston Marathon bombing on April 15, 2013, which resulted in the identification and capture of the perpetrators.",
