      "text": "The wreckage of Malaysia Airlines Flight 17 was found near the village of Hrabove in Donetsk Oblast, Ukraine, approximately 40 kilometers from the Ukraine-Russia border.",
      "date": "2014-07-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Casualties Confirmed",
      "text": "All 283 passengers and 15 crew members on board Malaysia Airlines Flight 17 were confirmed dead following the shoot-down on July 17, 2014.",
      "date": "2014-07-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "International Investigation Launched",
      "text": "An international investigation into the downing of Malaysia Airlines Flight 17 was launched, involving multiple countries and organizations.",
      "date": "2014-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dutch Safety Board Report",
      "text": "In October 2015, the Dutch Safety Board released a report concluding that Malaysia Airlines Flight 17 was shot down by a Buk missile fired from an area controlled by pro-Russian rebels.",
      "date": "2015-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Criminal Investigation Findings",
      "text": "In June 2019, the Joint Investigation Team announced that four individuals would be charged with murder for their involvement in the downing of Malaysia Airlines Flight 17.",
      "date": "2019-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Trial Begins",
      "text": "The trial of the four individuals charged with the downing of Malaysia Airlines Flight 17 began in the Netherlands on March 9, 2020.",
