      "text": "Tutankhamun was born around 1341 BCE. He was originally named Tutankhaten, reflecting the worship of the Aten, the sun disk.",
      "date": "-1341"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ascension to the Throne",
      "text": "Tutankhamun became pharaoh around 1332 BCE, at the age of about nine, following the death of Akhenaten and the brief reign of Smenkhkare.",
      "date": "-1332"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marriage to Ankhesenamun",
      "text": "Tutankhamun married Ankhesenamun, his half-sister and the daughter of Akhenaten and Nefertiti, shortly after his ascension to the throne.",
      "date": "-1332"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Restoration of Traditional Religion",
      "text": "During his reign, Tutankhamun restored the traditional polytheistic religion of Egypt, moving away from the monotheistic worship of Aten established by Akhenaten.",
      "date": "-1330"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Change of Name",
      "text": "Tutankhamun changed his name from Tutankhaten to Tutankhamun, reflecting the return to the worship of Amun, a major deity in the Egyptian pantheon.",
      "date": "-1330"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Tutankhamun",
      "text": "Tutankhamun died around 1323 BCE at the age of about 18 or 19. The cause of his death remains a subject of debate among historians and scientists.",
      "date": "-1323"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discovery of Tutankhamun's Tomb",
      "text": "Tutankhamun's tomb was discovered by Howard Carter in 1922, nearly intact, in the Valley of the Kings. This discovery sparked worldwide interest in ancient Egypt.",
      "date": "1922"
    }
  ]
}

