      "headline": "Birth of Mahavira",
      "text": "Mahavira, the 24th and last Tirthankara of the current time cycle, was born around 599 BCE in the kingdom of Vaishali (present-day Bihar, India).",
      "date": "-0599"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mahavira's Renunciation",
      "text": "At the age of 30, Mahavira renounced his worldly life and became an ascetic, embarking on a spiritual quest for liberation.",
      "date": "-0569"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mahavira's Enlightenment",
      "text": "After 12 years of rigorous penance and meditation, Mahavira attained Kevala Jnana (omniscience) in 527 BCE, becoming a Jina (conqueror).",
