    {
      "headline": "First Solo Nonstop Transatlantic Flight",
      "text": "On May 20-21, 1927, Charles Lindbergh made the first solo nonstop transatlantic flight from New York City to Paris. He flew the Spirit of St. Louis for 33.5 hours, covering a distance of 3,600 miles (5,800 km).",
