      "headline": "IEEE 802.11 Standard Released",
      "text": "In 1997, the first version of the IEEE 802.11 standard was released, providing 2 Mbit/s link speeds.",
      "date": "1997"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Wi-Fi Alliance Formed",
      "text": "In 1999, the Wi-Fi Alliance was formed as a trade association to hold the Wi-Fi trademark under which most products are sold.",
      "date": "1999"
    },
    {
      "headline": "IEEE 802.11b Standard Released",
      "text": "In 1999, the IEEE 802.11b standard was released, providing 11 Mbit/s link speeds and operating in the 2.4 GHz band.",
      "date": "1999"
    },
    {
      "headline": "IEEE 802.11a Standard Released",
      "text": "In 1999, the IEEE 802.11a standard was released, offering up to 54 Mbit/s link speeds and operating in the 5 GHz band.",
      "date": "1999"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Wi-Fi Protected Access (WPA) Introduced",
      "text": "In 2003, Wi-Fi Protected Access (WPA) was introduced as a security protocol to secure wireless computer networks.",
      "date": "2003"
    },
    {
      "headline": "IEEE 802.11g Standard Released",
      "text": "In 2003, the IEEE 802.11g standard was released, combining the best of 802.11a and 802.11b, providing 54 Mbit/s link speeds in the 2.4 GHz band.",
      "date": "2003"
    },
    {
      "headline": "IEEE 802.11n Standard Released",
      "text": "In 2009, the IEEE 802.11n standard was released, offering higher throughput improvements using multiple-input multiple-output antennas.",
      "date": "2009"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Wi-Fi Direct Introduced",
      "text": "In 2010, Wi-Fi Direct was introduced, allowing Wi-Fi devices to connect to each other without a wireless access point.",
      "date": "2010"
    },
    {
      "headline": "IEEE 802.11ac Standard Released",
      "text": "In 2013, the IEEE 802.11ac standard was released, providing high-throughput wireless local area networks on the 5 GHz band.",
      "date": "2013"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Wi-Fi 6 (IEEE 802.11ax) Released",
      "text": "In 2019, Wi-Fi 6, based on the IEEE 802.11ax standard, was released, improving average throughput per user by four times in dense or congested environments.",
      "date": "2019"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Wi-Fi 6E Introduced",
      "text": "In 2020, Wi-Fi 6E was introduced, extending Wi-Fi 6 into the 6 GHz band, providing additional spectrum for faster and more reliable connections.",
      "date": "2020"
    }
  ]
}

