      "headline": "Big Bang",
      "text": "The universe began with the Big Bang, approximately 13.787 billion years ago. This event marks the origin of space and time, and the universe has been expanding since then.",
      "date": "-13787000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the First Atoms",
      "text": "Around 380,000 years after the Big Bang, the universe cooled enough for electrons and protons to combine and form the first atoms, primarily hydrogen and helium. This period is known as recombination.",
      "date": "-13786620000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the First Stars and Galaxies",
      "text": "Approximately 100 to 200 million years after the Big Bang, the first stars and galaxies began to form, marking the end of the cosmic dark ages.",
      "date": "-13785000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Milky Way Galaxy",
      "text": "The Milky Way galaxy, which contains our solar system, began forming around 13.6 billion years ago.",
      "date": "-13600000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Solar System",
      "text": "The solar system, including Earth, formed about 4.6 billion years ago from the gravitational collapse of a region within a large molecular cloud.",
      "date": "-4600000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Appearance of Life on Earth",
      "text": "Life on Earth began approximately 3.5 billion years ago, with the emergence of simple, single-celled organisms.",
      "date": "-3500000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cambrian Explosion",
      "text": "Around 541 million years ago, the Cambrian Explosion occurred, a period of rapid evolutionary development and diversification of life forms.",
      "date": "-541000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Extinction of the Dinosaurs",
      "text": "Approximately 66 million years ago, a mass extinction event led to the extinction of the dinosaurs, likely caused by a massive asteroid impact.",
      "date": "-66000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rise of Homo Sapiens",
      "text": "Modern humans, Homo sapiens, first appeared around 300,000 years ago in Africa.",
      "date": "-300000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Modern Cosmology",
      "text": "In the early 20th century, modern cosmology emerged, establishing the Big Bang theory and the expanding universe model.",
