      "headline": "First Descriptions of DID",
      "text": "The first documented case of what is now known as dissociative identity disorder was reported in the 18th century. Early descriptions focused on symptoms of amnesia and multiple identities.",
      "date": "1700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Recognition in Psychiatry",
      "text": "In the late 19th century, cases of multiple personality disorder began to be recognized in the field of psychiatry, with notable cases such as that of Louis Vivet.",
      "date": "1880"
