      "headline": "Publication of 'The Asexual Manifesto'",
      "text": "In 2002, 'The Asexual Manifesto' was published by the Asexual Visibility and Education Network (AVEN), which helped to define and promote understanding of asexuality as a sexual orientation.",
      "date": "2002"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Founding of AVEN",
      "text": "The Asexual Visibility and Education Network (AVEN) was founded by David Jay in 2001. AVEN is one of the largest asexual communities and aims to create public acceptance and discussion of asexuality.",
      "date": "2001"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Asexuality in the DSM-5",
      "text": "In 2013, the American Psychiatric Association released the DSM-5, which included a note that asexuality should not be considered a disorder, helping to further legitimize asexuality as a valid sexual orientation.",
      "date": "2013"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Asexuality Awareness Week",
      "text": "Asexuality Awareness Week was first celebrated in 2010. It is an annual event that aims to educate about asexuality and promote acceptance of asexual individuals.",
      "date": "2010"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Inclusion in Pride Parades",
      "text": "Throughout the 2010s, asexuality gained more visibility and inclusion in LGBTQ+ pride parades and events around the world, highlighting the growing recognition of asexuality within the broader LGBTQ+ community.",
      "date": "2010"
    }
  ]
}

