      "headline": "Birth of Augustine",
      "text": "Augustine was born on November 13, 354, in Thagaste, a Roman province in North Africa, which is present-day Souk Ahras, Algeria.",
      "date": "0354-11-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Education in Carthage",
      "text": "In 370, Augustine went to Carthage to continue his education in rhetoric.",
      "date": "0370"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Conversion to Manichaeism",
      "text": "Around 373, Augustine became a follower of Manichaeism, a major religious movement founded by the prophet Mani.",
      "date": "0373"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Teaching in Rome and Milan",
      "text": "In 383, Augustine moved to Rome to teach rhetoric and then to Milan in 384, where he became a professor of rhetoric.",
      "date": "0383"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Conversion to Christianity",
      "text": "In 386, Augustine converted to Christianity, influenced by the preaching of Ambrose, the bishop of Milan.",
      "date": "0386"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Baptism by Ambrose",
      "text": "Augustine was baptized by Ambrose in Milan during Easter, April 24-25, 387.",
      "date": "0387-04-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return to Africa",
      "text": "In 388, Augustine returned to North Africa with the intention of establishing a monastic community.",
      "date": "0388"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ordination as Priest",
      "text": "In 391, Augustine was ordained as a priest in Hippo Regius, present-day Annaba, Algeria.",
      "date": "0391"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Becomes Bishop of Hippo",
      "text": "In 395, Augustine was made the Bishop of Hippo, a position he held until his death.",
      "date": "0395"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Writing of 'Confessions'",
      "text": "Between 397 and 400, Augustine wrote 'Confessions', an autobiographical work outlining his sinful youth and conversion to Christianity.",
      "date": "0397"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Writing of 'The City of God'",
      "text": "Augustine began writing 'The City of God' in 413, a work that defended Christianity against pagan critics and outlined a Christian philosophy of history.",
      "date": "0413"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Augustine",
      "text": "Augustine died on August 28, 430, during the siege of Hippo by the Vandals.",
      "date": "0430-08-28"
    }
  ]
}

