      "headline": "Coronation as Tsar of All Russia",
      "text": "On January 16, 1547, Ivan IV was crowned as the first Tsar of All Russia, marking the transformation of the Russian state.",
      "date": "1547-01-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marriage to Anastasia Romanovna",
      "text": "Ivan IV married Anastasia Romanovna on February 3, 1547, who became his first wife and the first Tsaritsa of Russia.",
      "date": "1547-02-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reforms and the Creation of the Oprichnina",
      "text": "In 1565, Ivan IV established the Oprichnina, a policy that involved the creation of a separate territory within Russia governed directly by the Tsar and policed by his personal army.",
      "date": "1565"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Anastasia Romanovna",
      "text": "Anastasia Romanovna, Ivan IV's first wife, died on August 7, 1560, which deeply affected Ivan and led to increased paranoia and tyranny.",
      "date": "1560-08-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ivan's Mental Health Declines",
      "text": "Ivan IV's mental health began to decline significantly after the death of his wife, leading to increased violence and erratic behavior.",
      "date": "1560"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ivan Kills His Son",
      "text": "In a fit of rage, Ivan IV killed his son and heir, Ivan Ivanovich, on November 19, 1581, which left the Tsardom without a competent heir.",
      "date": "1581-11-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Ivan the Terrible",
      "text": "Ivan IV died on March 28, 1584, in Moscow, leaving behind a legacy of expansion and terror.",
      "date": "1584-03-28"
    }
  ]
}

