      "headline": "First Major Milestone",
      "text": "The DJIA reached its first major milestone by closing above 100 points for the first time on January 12, 1906.",
      "date": "1906-01-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Stock Market Crash of 1929",
      "text": "The DJIA experienced a significant crash beginning on October 24, 1929, known as Black Thursday, marking the start of the Great Depression.",
      "date": "1929-10-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Post-World War II Recovery",
      "text": "After World War II, the DJIA began a period of recovery and growth, reaching a new high of 381.17 on November 23, 1954, surpassing its pre-1929 crash high.",
      "date": "1954-11-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Black Monday",
      "text": "On October 19, 1987, the DJIA suffered its largest one-day percentage drop in history, losing 22.61% of its value.",
      "date": "1987-10-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dot-com Bubble Peak",
      "text": "The DJIA reached a peak during the dot-com bubble, closing above 11,000 for the first time on May 3, 1999.",
      "date": "1999-05-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Impact of the 2008 Financial Crisis",
      "text": "The DJIA experienced significant losses during the 2008 financial crisis, dropping to a low of 6,547.05 on March 9, 2009.",
      "date": "2009-03-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Record Highs in the 2010s",
      "text": "Throughout the 2010s, the DJIA reached several record highs, closing above 20,000 for the first time on January 25, 2017.",
      "date": "2017-01-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "COVID-19 Pandemic Impact",
      "text": "The DJIA experienced significant volatility during the COVID-19 pandemic, with a notable drop in March 2020, but later recovered to reach new highs.",
      "date": "2020-03"
    }
  ]
}

