      "text": "On January 14, 2011, Tunisian President Zine El Abidine Ben Ali fled to Saudi Arabia after 23 years in power, marking the first successful ousting of a leader during the Arab Spring.",
      "date": "2011-01-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Egyptian Revolution Begins",
      "text": "On January 25, 2011, mass protests began in Egypt, demanding the end of President Hosni Mubarak's regime, inspired by the events in Tunisia.",
      "date": "2011-01-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hosni Mubarak Resigns",
      "text": "On February 11, 2011, Egyptian President Hosni Mubarak resigned after 18 days of mass protests, ending his 30-year rule.",
      "date": "2011-02-11"
    },
