      "headline": "Construction Begins",
      "text": "Construction of the Alhambra began in 1238 under the Nasrid emir Mohammed I Ibn al-Ahmar, the founder of the Nasrid dynasty, who established the royal residence on the Sabika hill.",
      "date": "1238"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the Alcazaba",
      "text": "The Alcazaba, the oldest part of the Alhambra, was completed around 1273. It served as a military fortress and was one of the first structures built during the initial phase of construction.",
      "date": "1273"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of Yusuf I",
      "text": "During the reign of Yusuf I (1333-1354), significant additions were made to the Alhambra, including the Comares Palace and the Hall of the Ambassadors.",
      "date": "1333"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of Muhammad V",
      "text": "Muhammad V (1354-1391) continued the expansion and embellishment of the Alhambra, including the construction of the iconic Court of the Lions and the Hall of the Abencerrajes.",
      "date": "1354"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the Palace of the Lions",
      "text": "The Palace of the Lions, one of the most famous parts of the Alhambra, was completed during the reign of Muhammad V.",
      "date": "1380"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fall of Granada",
      "text": "In 1492, the Alhambra was surrendered to the Catholic Monarchs, Ferdinand and Isabella, marking the end of Muslim rule in Spain.",
      "date": "1492"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Charles V's Palace",
      "text": "In 1526, Charles V ordered the construction of a Renaissance-style palace within the Alhambra complex, which was never fully completed.",
      "date": "1526"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Alhambra Decree",
      "text": "The Alhambra Decree, issued in 1492, ordered the expulsion of practicing Jews from the Kingdoms of Castile and Aragon, which was signed at the Alhambra.",
      "date": "1492"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Restoration Efforts",
      "text": "In the 19th century, the Alhambra underwent significant restoration efforts to preserve its historical and architectural integrity.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "UNESCO World Heritage Site",
      "text": "In 1984, the Alhambra was declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site, recognizing its cultural and historical significance.",
      "date": "1984"
    }
  ]
}

