      "headline": "Original Proposal of the Monty Hall Problem",
      "text": "The Monty Hall problem was originally posed in a letter by Steve Selvin to the American Statistician in 1975.",
      "date": "1975"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication in Parade Magazine",
      "text": "The Monty Hall problem became famous as a question from reader Craig F. Whitaker's letter quoted in Marilyn vos Savant's 'Ask Marilyn' column in Parade magazine in 1990.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Widespread Public Debate",
      "text": "Following its publication in Parade magazine, the Monty Hall problem sparked widespread public debate and discussion, particularly regarding the counterintuitive nature of the solution.",
