      "headline": "Origins of Taekwondo",
      "text": "Taekwondo's origins can be traced back to traditional Korean martial arts such as Taekkyeon, Subak, and Gwonbeop, which were practiced during the Three Kingdoms period in Korea.",
      "date": "-0057"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Modern Taekwondo",
      "text": "The development of modern Taekwondo began in the 1940s and 1950s after the end of Japanese occupation in Korea. Various martial arts schools (kwans) were established, each with its own style.",
      "date": "1940"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of Korea Taekwondo Association",
      "text": "In 1959, the Korea Taekwondo Association (KTA) was formed to unify the various martial arts schools and standardize Taekwondo practices.",
      "date": "1959"
    },
    {
      "headline": "International Taekwondo Federation (ITF) Established",
      "text": "The International Taekwondo Federation (ITF) was founded in 1966 by General Choi Hong Hi to promote Taekwondo worldwide.",
      "date": "1966"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World Taekwondo Federation (WTF) Established",
      "text": "The World Taekwondo Federation (WTF), now known as World Taekwondo (WT), was established in 1973 to further globalize the sport and organize international competitions.",
      "date": "1973"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First World Taekwondo Championships",
      "text": "The first World Taekwondo Championships were held in Seoul, South Korea, in 1973, marking a significant milestone in the sport's international recognition.",
      "date": "1973"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Taekwondo Becomes an Olympic Sport",
      "text": "Taekwondo was included as a demonstration sport in the 1988 Seoul Olympics and became an official Olympic sport in the 2000 Sydney Olympics.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Renaming of World Taekwondo Federation",
      "text": "In 2017, the World Taekwondo Federation officially changed its name to World Taekwondo to avoid negative connotations associated with the acronym WTF.",
      "date": "2017"
    }
  ]
}

