      "headline": "Construction of the Colossus of Rhodes",
      "text": "The Colossus of Rhodes was constructed by Chares of Lindos in 280 BCE. It was a statue of the Greek sun god Helios, erected in the city of Rhodes to celebrate the successful defense of the city against an attack by Demetrius I of Macedon.",
      "date": "-0280"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Destruction by Earthquake",
      "text": "In 226 BCE, the Colossus of Rhodes was destroyed by an earthquake. The statue broke at the knees and fell over onto the land.",
      "date": "-0226"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Remains Left Undisturbed",
      "text": "After its destruction, the remains of the Colossus lay on the ground for over 800 years. The Rhodians received an oracle that advised them not to rebuild it.",
      "date": "-0226"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sale of the Remains",
      "text": "In 654 CE, the remains of the Colossus were sold by the Arabs who had captured Rhodes. It is said that the remains were sold to a Jewish merchant from Edessa, who transported the bronze on 900 camels.",
      "date": "0654"
    }
  ]
}

