      "text": "The Convention Concerning the Protection of the World Cultural and Natural Heritage was adopted by the General Conference of UNESCO on November 16, 1972. This treaty established the framework for the identification, protection, and preservation of cultural and natural heritage around the world.",
      "date": "1972-11-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First World Heritage Sites Inscribed",
      "text": "In 1978, the first World Heritage Sites were inscribed. These included the Galápagos Islands in Ecuador, the city of Quito in Ecuador, and the Aachen Cathedral in Germany, among others.",
      "date": "1978"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World Heritage Committee Established",
      "text": "The World Heritage Committee was established to oversee the implementation of the World Heritage Convention and to decide on the inscription of sites on the World Heritage List.",
      "date": "1976"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World Heritage in Danger List Introduced",
      "text": "In 1992, the List of World Heritage in Danger was introduced to identify sites that are threatened by serious and specific dangers, such as armed conflict, natural disasters, or urbanization.",
      "date": "1992"
    },
    {
      "headline": "200th World Heritage Site Inscribed",
      "text": "In 1994, the 200th World Heritage Site was inscribed, marking a significant milestone in the expansion of the World Heritage List.",
      "date": "1994"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World Heritage Convention's 30th Anniversary",
      "text": "In 2002, UNESCO celebrated the 30th anniversary of the World Heritage Convention, highlighting the achievements and challenges in the protection of cultural and natural heritage.",
      "date": "2002"
    },
    {
      "headline": "1000th World Heritage Site Inscribed",
      "text": "In 2014, the 1000th World Heritage Site was inscribed, showcasing the growing recognition of sites of outstanding universal value.",
      "date": "2014"
    }
  ]
}

