      "text": "William McKinley's victory in the 1900 election made him the eighth president to win consecutive re-election and the first since Ulysses S. Grant accomplished the same feat in 1872.",
      "date": "1900-11-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Historical Context of the Election",
      "text": "Until 1956, this would be the last time in which an incumbent Republican president would win re-election after serving a full term in office.",
