      "headline": "Leader of the Opposition",
      "text": "After his defeat, Trudeau served as the leader of the Opposition from 1979 to 1980.",
      "date": "1979"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return as Prime Minister",
      "text": "Pierre Trudeau returned as Prime Minister of Canada on March 3, 1980, after winning the federal election.",
      "date": "1980-03-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Patriation of the Constitution",
      "text": "In 1982, Trudeau successfully patriated the Canadian Constitution and introduced the Charter of Rights and Freedoms.",
