      "headline": "First establishment as a religious site",
      "text": "In 708, Aubert, Bishop of Avranches, founded a sanctuary on Mont-Tombe after having a vision of the Archangel Michael.",
      "date": "0708"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the first abbey",
      "text": "In 966, the Benedictine monks settled on the rock at the request of the Duke of Normandy, Richard I, and began construction of the first abbey.",
      "date": "0966"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Romanesque Abbey Church construction",
      "text": "In 1023, construction of the Romanesque Abbey Church began, which was completed in 1084.",
      "date": "1023"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the Romanesque Abbey Church",
      "text": "In 1084, the Romanesque Abbey Church was completed, marking a significant architectural achievement.",
      "date": "1084"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Gothic additions",
      "text": "In 1204, after a fire, the abbey was rebuilt in the Gothic style, including the addition of the Merveille (Marvel), a series of buildings on the north side.",
      "date": "1204"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hundred Years' War fortifications",
      "text": "During the Hundred Years' War (1337-1453), Mont-Saint-Michel was fortified to withstand sieges, becoming a symbol of French national identity.",
      "date": "1337"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dissolution of the monastery",
      "text": "In 1791, during the French Revolution, the monastery was dissolved, and the site was used as a prison.",
      "date": "1791"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Prison closure",
      "text": "In 1863, the prison was closed, and efforts to restore the abbey began.",
      "date": "1863"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Declared a historic monument",
      "text": "In 1874, Mont-Saint-Michel was declared a historic monument, leading to restoration efforts.",
      "date": "1874"
    },
    {
      "headline": "UNESCO World Heritage Site designation",
      "text": "In 1979, Mont-Saint-Michel and its bay were designated as a UNESCO World Heritage Site.",
      "date": "1979"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the new bridge",
      "text": "In 2014, a new bridge was completed to replace the causeway, allowing the island to be surrounded by water again.",
      "date": "2014"
    }
  ]
}

