      "headline": "Emergency Proclaimed",
      "text": "On June 25, 1975, a state of emergency was declared in India, which lasted until March 21, 1977. During this period, the powers of the Parliament were significantly altered.",
      "date": "1975-06-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "44th Amendment Act",
      "text": "The 44th Amendment Act was enacted on April 30, 1979, which restored the original balance of power between the Parliament and the judiciary, reversing many changes made during the Emergency.",
      "date": "1979-04-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Anti-Defection Law",
      "text": "The Anti-Defection Law was introduced by the 52nd Amendment to the Constitution in 1985, to prevent political defections and ensure stability in the Parliament.",
