      "text": "In 1893, Caleb Bradham, a pharmacist in New Bern, North Carolina, created a drink called 'Brad's Drink' which was a mix of sugar, water, caramel, lemon oil, nutmeg, and other natural additives.",
      "date": "1893"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Renaming to Pepsi-Cola",
      "text": "On August 28, 1898, Caleb Bradham renamed his drink 'Pepsi-Cola'. The name was chosen to reflect the drink's supposed health benefits, as it was advertised to relieve dyspepsia (indigestion) and its cola flavor.",
      "date": "1898-08-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Pepsi-Cola Company Incorporation",
      "text": "In 1902, Caleb Bradham incorporated the Pepsi-Cola Company in North Carolina.",
      "date": "1902"
