      "headline": "Sinking of the USS Maine",
      "text": "On February 15, 1898, the USS Maine exploded and sank in Havana Harbor, Cuba. This event escalated tensions between the United States and Spain, contributing to the outbreak of the Spanish–American War.",
      "date": "1898-02-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "U.S. Declaration of War on Spain",
      "text": "On April 25, 1898, the United States formally declared war on Spain, marking the official start of the Spanish–American War.",
      "date": "1898-04-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Manila Bay",
      "text": "On May 1, 1898, the U.S. Navy, led by Commodore George Dewey, defeated the Spanish fleet in Manila Bay, Philippines. This victory was a significant early success for the United States.",
      "date": "1898-05-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of San Juan Hill",
      "text": "On July 1, 1898, U.S. forces, including the Rough Riders led by Theodore Roosevelt, captured San Juan Hill in Cuba. This battle was a pivotal moment in the Cuban campaign.",
      "date": "1898-07-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Surrender of Santiago",
      "text": "On July 17, 1898, Spanish forces in Santiago, Cuba, surrendered to the United States, effectively ending major hostilities in Cuba.",
      "date": "1898-07-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Capture of Puerto Rico",
      "text": "On July 25, 1898, U.S. forces landed in Puerto Rico and quickly took control of the island, which was a Spanish territory.",
      "date": "1898-07-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Protocol of Peace",
      "text": "On August 12, 1898, the United States and Spain signed a Protocol of Peace, agreeing to cease hostilities and begin negotiations for a formal peace treaty.",
      "date": "1898-08-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Paris",
      "text": "On December 10, 1898, the Treaty of Paris was signed, officially ending the Spanish–American War. Spain ceded Puerto Rico, Guam, and the Philippines to the United States, and relinquished its claim to Cuba.",
      "date": "1898-12-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ratification of the Treaty of Paris",
      "text": "On February 6, 1899, the U.S. Senate ratified the Treaty of Paris, finalizing the terms of peace and the acquisition of new territories.",
      "date": "1899-02-06"
    }
  ]
}

