      "headline": "Central Park Birdwatching Incident",
      "text": "On May 25, 2020, the Central Park birdwatching incident occurred, where a woman named Amy Cooper called the police on a Black birdwatcher, Christian Cooper, in Central Park, New York. This incident was widely publicized and contributed to the popularization of the 'Karen' stereotype.",
      "date": "2020-05-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Increased Usage During COVID-19 Pandemic",
      "text": "During the COVID-19 pandemic, the term 'Karen' saw increased usage to describe individuals who refused to follow public health guidelines, such as wearing masks or social distancing.",
