      "headline": "Establishment of the Medal of Honor",
      "text": "The Medal of Honor was first established by the United States Navy on December 21, 1861, during the American Civil War. It was created to recognize acts of valor by sailors and marines.",
      "date": "1861-12-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Army Medal of Honor Authorized",
      "text": "On July 12, 1862, the United States Army authorized its own version of the Medal of Honor, expanding the recognition to include acts of valor by soldiers.",
