      "text": "On March 9-10, 1945, B-29s conducted Operation Meetinghouse, a massive incendiary bombing raid on Tokyo, resulting in extensive destruction and significant civilian casualties.",
      "date": "1945-03-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Atomic Bombing of Hiroshima",
      "text": "On August 6, 1945, the B-29 Superfortress Enola Gay dropped the first atomic bomb, 'Little Boy,' on Hiroshima, Japan, marking a pivotal moment in World War II.",
      "date": "1945-08-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Atomic Bombing of Nagasaki",
      "text": "On August 9, 1945, the B-29 Superfortress Bockscar dropped the second atomic bomb, 'Fat Man,' on Nagasaki, Japan, leading to Japan's surrender and the end of World War II.",
      "date": "1945-08-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Production",
      "text": "Production of the B-29 Superfortress ended in 1946, with a total of 3,970 units built.",
      "date": "1946"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Service in the Korean War",
      "text": "The B-29 Superfortress was used extensively during the Korean War from 1950 to 1953, performing bombing missions and reconnaissance.",
      "date": "1950"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Retirement from Active Service",
      "text": "The B-29 Superfortress was retired from active service in the United States Air Force in 1960, marking the end of its operational use.",
      "date": "1960"
    }
  ]
}

