    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Binomial Nomenclature",
      "text": "In 1753, Carl Linnaeus introduced the binomial nomenclature system in his work 'Species Plantarum', which became the standard for naming species.",
      "date": "1753"
    },
    {
      "headline": "10th Edition of Systema Naturae",
      "text": "In 1758, the 10th edition of 'Systema Naturae' was published, which is considered the starting point for zoological nomenclature.",
