      "headline": "Origin of the Hamburger Name",
      "text": "The name 'hamburger' originates from the city of Hamburg, Germany. In the 19th century, Hamburg was known for its beef, and the term 'Hamburg steak' was used to describe a patty made from minced beef.",
      "date": "1800"
