      "text": "On April 6, 1793, the National Convention established the Committee of Public Safety, which would later play a central role in the Reign of Terror.",
      "date": "1793-04-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Execution of King Louis XVI",
      "text": "King Louis XVI was executed by guillotine on January 21, 1793, marking a significant escalation in revolutionary fervor.",
      "date": "1793-01-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Start of the Reign of Terror",
      "text": "The Reign of Terror officially began on September 5, 1793, when the National Convention declared terror 'the order of the day.'",
      "date": "1793-09-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Law of Suspects",
      "text": "On September 17, 1793, the Law of Suspects was enacted, allowing for the arrest of individuals deemed counter-revolutionary.",
