      "headline": "American Civil War",
      "text": "During the American Civil War (1861-1865), the Mississippi River was a strategic asset, with control of the river being crucial for both the Union and Confederate forces.",
      "date": "1861"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Great Mississippi Flood of 1927",
      "text": "In 1927, the Mississippi River experienced one of the most devastating floods in U.S. history, affecting hundreds of thousands of people and leading to significant changes in flood control policies.",
      "date": "1927"
    },
