      "text": "In the late 11th century, the renowned Islamic theologian and philosopher Al-Ghazali wrote extensively on Sufism, integrating it with mainstream Islamic thought. His works, such as 'The Revival of the Religious Sciences,' helped legitimize Sufism within the broader Islamic community.",
      "date": "1090"
