      "text": "The Ming dynasty (1368–1644) saw eunuchs reach the height of their power. They controlled the imperial household and had significant influence over the emperor.",
      "date": "1368"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Zheng He's Voyages",
      "text": "Zheng He, a famous Chinese eunuch, led seven maritime expeditions between 1405 and 1433 during the Ming dynasty, expanding China's influence across Asia and Africa.",
      "date": "1405"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decline of Eunuchs in the Qing Dynasty",
      "text": "During the Qing dynasty (1644–1912), the power of eunuchs began to decline. The Qing emperors implemented reforms to reduce their influence.",
      "date": "1644"
