      "text": "In June 2017, ISKP fighters captured the Tora Bora complex in eastern Afghanistan, a strategic location previously used by Al-Qaeda.",
      "date": "2017-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Kabul Hospital Attack",
      "text": "On March 8, 2017, ISKP claimed responsibility for an attack on a military hospital in Kabul, Afghanistan, which resulted in the deaths of at least 49 people.",
      "date": "2017-03-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Attack on Sikh Temple in Kabul",
      "text": "On March 25, 2020, ISKP attacked a Sikh temple in Kabul, killing 25 worshippers. This attack highlighted the group's ongoing threat to religious minorities in the region.",
      "date": "2020-03-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Kabul Airport Bombing",
      "text": "On August 26, 2021, ISKP carried out a suicide bombing at Kabul's Hamid Karzai International Airport, killing 13 U.S. service members and at least 170 Afghan civilians during the U.S. withdrawal from Afghanistan.",
      "date": "2021-08-26"
    }
  ]
}

