      "headline": "Psilocybin Research in the 1960s",
      "text": "During the 1960s, psilocybin was widely studied for its potential therapeutic effects, particularly in the treatment of mental health disorders.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Controlled Substance Classification",
      "text": "In 1970, psilocybin was classified as a Schedule I controlled substance in the United States under the Controlled Substances Act, severely restricting its use and research.",
      "date": "1970"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Renewed Interest in Psilocybin Research",
      "text": "In the 1990s, interest in psilocybin research was renewed, leading to a resurgence of studies exploring its potential therapeutic benefits.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Psilocybin-Assisted Therapy Studies",
      "text": "In the 2000s and 2010s, numerous studies were conducted on psilocybin-assisted therapy, showing promise in treating conditions such as depression, anxiety, and PTSD.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
