      "headline": "Emergence of Populism",
      "text": "Populism as a political concept began to emerge in the late 19th century, particularly with the rise of the People's Party in the United States, which was founded in 1891. This party sought to represent the interests of farmers and laborers against the economic elite.",
      "date": "1891"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Populism in Russia",
      "text": "In the late 19th century, the term 'populism' was also used to describe the Russian Narodnik movement, which sought to mobilize the peasantry against the ruling elite.",
