      "text": "Osaka's history dates back to the 5th century when it was known as Naniwa. It became a significant port city and a gateway to the Korean Peninsula and China.",
      "date": "-0500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Naniwa as Capital",
      "text": "In 645, Emperor Kōtoku established Naniwa as the capital of Japan, making it the first capital city of Japan.",
