      "text": "The Harrison Narcotics Tax Act was passed in 1914 in the United States, which regulated and taxed the production, importation, and distribution of opiates and coca products, including heroin.",
      "date": "1914"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Heroin Banned in the United States",
      "text": "In 1924, the United States Congress banned the manufacture, sale, and importation of heroin.",
      "date": "1924"
