      "headline": "Code Name 'Trinity' Assigned",
      "text": "The code name 'Trinity' was assigned by J. Robert Oppenheimer, the director of the Los Alamos Laboratory, possibly inspired by the poetry of John Donne.",
      "date": "1944"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Trinity Nuclear Test",
      "text": "Trinity was the code name of the first detonation of a nuclear weapon, conducted by the United States Army at 5:29 a.m. MWT on July 16, 1945, as part of the Manhattan Project. The test was of an implosion-design plutonium bomb, nicknamed 'The Gadget'.",
      "date": "1945-07-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fat Man Bomb Detonated Over Nagasaki",
      "text": "The Fat Man bomb, which was of the same design as 'The Gadget' tested during the Trinity nuclear test, was detonated over Nagasaki, Japan, on August 9, 1945.",
      "date": "1945-08-09"
    }
  ]
}

