    {
      "headline": "Issuance of the Great Charter of 1225",
      "text": "In 1225, Henry III issued a revised version of the Magna Carta, known as the Great Charter of 1225, which limited royal power and protected the rights of the major barons.",
      "date": "1225"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Failed Invasion of France",
      "text": "In 1230, Henry III attempted to reconquer the provinces of France that had once belonged to his father, but the invasion ended in failure.",
      "date": "1230"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Revolt Led by Richard Marshal",
      "text": "A revolt led by Richard Marshal, son of William Marshal, broke out in 1232. It ended in a peace settlement negotiated by the Church.",
      "date": "1232"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Henry III",
      "text": "Henry III died on November 16, 1272, in Westminster, London, England. He was succeeded by his son, Edward I.",
