      "text": "Construction of Hadrian's Wall began in AD 122 during the reign of Emperor Hadrian. The wall was intended to defend the Roman province of Britannia from the tribes to the north.",
      "date": "0122"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of Hadrian's Wall",
      "text": "The construction of Hadrian's Wall was largely completed by around AD 128. The wall stretched from Wallsend on the River Tyne in the east to Bowness-on-Solway in the west.",
      "date": "0128"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Antonine Wall Constructed",
      "text": "In AD 142, the Romans began constructing the Antonine Wall further north in Scotland, which temporarily superseded Hadrian's Wall as the northern frontier of Roman Britain.",
      "date": "0142"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reoccupation of Hadrian's Wall",
      "text": "After the abandonment of the Antonine Wall around AD 162, Hadrian's Wall was reoccupied and once again became the main defensive fortification in the north of Roman Britain.",
      "date": "0162"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Severan Rebuilding",
      "text": "During the reign of Emperor Septimius Severus, around AD 208-211, Hadrian's Wall underwent significant repairs and rebuilding efforts.",
      "date": "0208"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Roman Withdrawal from Britain",
      "text": "By AD 410, Roman forces had withdrawn from Britain, leading to the abandonment of Hadrian's Wall as a military fortification.",
      "date": "0410"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Designation as a UNESCO World Heritage Site",
      "text": "In 1987, Hadrian's Wall was designated as a UNESCO World Heritage Site, recognizing its historical significance and preservation.",
      "date": "1987"
    }
  ]
}

