      "headline": "Kansas Territory Established",
      "text": "The Kansas Territory was established on May 30, 1854, as part of the Kansas-Nebraska Act, which allowed the territories to decide on the legality of slavery through popular sovereignty.",
      "date": "1854-05-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bleeding Kansas",
      "text": "From 1854 to 1859, Kansas was the site of violent confrontations between pro-slavery and anti-slavery factions, known as Bleeding Kansas, which was a precursor to the American Civil War.",
      "date": "1854"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Kansas Admitted to the Union",
      "text": "Kansas was admitted to the Union as the 34th state on January 29, 1861, entering as a free state.",
      "date": "1861-01-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Topeka Becomes State Capital",
      "text": "Topeka was chosen as the capital of Kansas in 1861, shortly after the state was admitted to the Union.",
      "date": "1861"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Chisholm Trail",
      "text": "The Chisholm Trail, used from 1867 to 1884, was a major route for cattle drives from Texas to Kansas railheads.",
      "date": "1867"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Wichita Founded",
      "text": "The city of Wichita was officially incorporated in 1870, and it later became the most populous city in Kansas.",
      "date": "1870"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Kansas City, Kansas, Incorporated",
      "text": "Kansas City, Kansas, was incorporated in 1872, becoming part of the larger Kansas City metropolitan area.",
      "date": "1872"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Prohibition in Kansas",
      "text": "Kansas enacted statewide prohibition of alcohol in 1881, becoming the first state to do so, and it remained in effect until 1948.",
      "date": "1881"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Brown v. Board of Education",
      "text": "In 1954, the U.S. Supreme Court's decision in Brown v. Board of Education of Topeka declared racial segregation in public schools unconstitutional, a landmark case originating in Kansas.",
      "date": "1954"
