      "headline": "Beginning of the Victorian Era",
      "text": "The Victorian era began with the accession of Queen Victoria to the throne on 20 June 1837.",
      "date": "1837-06-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Great Exhibition",
      "text": "The Great Exhibition, also known as the Crystal Palace Exhibition, was held in Hyde Park, London, from 1 May to 15 October 1851. It was the first in a series of World's Fairs, exhibitions of culture and industry that became popular in the 19th century.",
      "date": "1851-05-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'On the Origin of Species'",
      "text": "Charles Darwin published 'On the Origin of Species' on 24 November 1859, introducing the scientific theory that populations evolve over generations through a process of natural selection.",
      "date": "1859-11-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Second Reform Act",
      "text": "The Second Reform Act was passed in 1867, significantly expanding the electorate in Britain by extending the vote to many working-class men.",
      "date": "1867"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the British North America Act",
      "text": "The British North America Act was enacted on 1 July 1867, creating the Dominion of Canada and marking a significant step in the development of the Canadian nation.",
      "date": "1867-07-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the Suez Canal",
      "text": "The Suez Canal was completed on 17 November 1869, providing a crucial maritime shortcut between Europe and Asia.",
      "date": "1869-11-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Education Act 1870",
      "text": "The Education Act of 1870, also known as the Forster Act, was passed to provide universal elementary education in England and Wales.",
      "date": "1870"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Queen Victoria's Golden Jubilee",
      "text": "Queen Victoria celebrated her Golden Jubilee on 20 June 1887, marking 50 years on the throne.",
      "date": "1887-06-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Queen Victoria's Diamond Jubilee",
      "text": "Queen Victoria celebrated her Diamond Jubilee on 22 June 1897, marking 60 years on the throne.",
      "date": "1897-06-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Victorian Era",
      "text": "The Victorian era ended with the death of Queen Victoria on 22 January 1901.",
